{"name":"Lol Yellow","hex":"#e7cd8b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lol","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Mongo."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Alternative form of LOL."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lol"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"LOL","blocks":[{"text":"LOL, or lol, is an acronym for \"laughing out loud\", and a popular element of Internet slang, which can be used to indicate amusement. It was first used almost exclusively on Usenet, but has since become widespread in other forms of computer-mediated communication and even face-to-face communication. It is one of many acronyms for expressing bodily reactions, in particular laughter, as text, including acronyms for more emphatic expressions of laughter such as LMAO and ROFL or ROTFL."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Lol_message_in_convo.jpg/330px-Lol_message_in_convo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LOL","wikidata":"Q2134"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Pratt_Inst_Library_editathon_2019-e_jeh_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Pratt_Inst_Library_editathon_2019-e_jeh_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Pratt_Inst_Library_editathon_2019-e_jeh_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Pratt_Inst_Library_editathon_2019-e_jeh_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Pratt_Inst_Library_editathon_2019-e_jeh_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Pratt_Inst_Library_editathon_2019-e_jeh_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A person literally laughing out loud in a university computer lab","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APratt_Inst_Library_editathon_2019-e_jeh_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Buesum_molenfeuer_lol_rofl.JPG/500px-Buesum_molenfeuer_lol_rofl.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Buesum_molenfeuer_lol_rofl.JPG/1280px-Buesum_molenfeuer_lol_rofl.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Buesum_molenfeuer_lol_rofl.JPG/500px-Buesum_molenfeuer_lol_rofl.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"2008 graffiti featuring LOL and ROFL on the Molenfeuer lighthouse in Büsum, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuesum_molenfeuer_lol_rofl.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f6/Omegalul_emote.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f6/Omegalul_emote.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The OMEGA­LUL Twitch emote is a distorted image of TotalBiscuit originating c. 2013.[37]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOmegalul_emote.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Lolwut_cat.jpg/500px-Lolwut_cat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Lolwut_cat.jpg/500px-Lolwut_cat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 2007 lolcat meme, featuring a humorous misspelling of \"LOL, what?\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALolwut_cat.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/73/Roflcopter.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/73/Roflcopter.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"An animated ASCII art image popularized in 2004 by memes using the word \"roflcopter\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoflcopter.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/